<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Token Launch Radar — pre-token protocols ranked by implied value</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="app.css">
</head>
<body>
<header class="top">
  <div>
    <h1>Token Launch Radar</h1>
    <p class="sub">Every protocol that records no token, ranked by what its launch would be worth — fitted from the traded tokens in the same snapshot, tested out of sample before a single row is ranked.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="meta" id="meta"></div>
</header>

<section class="strip" id="strip" aria-label="Validation summary"></section>

<nav class="controls">
  <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Search name or slug…" aria-label="Search protocols">
  <select id="cat" aria-label="Filter by category"><option value="">All categories</option></select>
  <select id="sort" aria-label="Sort board">
    <option value="rank">Sort: implied value</option>
    <option value="tvl">Sort: TVL</option>
    <option value="growth">Sort: 7-day growth</option>
    <option value="age">Sort: age</option>
    <option value="gas">Sort: cheapest farm gas</option>
  </select>
  <label class="check"><input id="wl" type="checkbox"> Watchlist only</label>
  <label class="check"><input id="early" type="checkbox"> Below the $50M floor only</label>
  <button id="viewBoard" class="view on">Board</button>
  <button id="viewLive" class="view">Live tokens</button>
</nav>

<main>
  <section id="boardWrap">
    <p class="count" id="count"></p>
    <table id="board">
      <thead><tr>
        <th>#</th><th>Protocol</th><th>Category</th><th>Chains</th>
        <th class="num">TVL</th><th class="num">7d</th><th class="num">Age</th>
        <th class="num">Implied value</th><th class="num">Multiple</th><th class="num">Farm gas</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody id="rows"></tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="hint">Click any row for its detail view: model breakdown, farm plan and net cost.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="detail" class="detail" hidden></section>

  <section id="liveWrap" hidden>
    <h2>Live tokens — the market's own values, kept apart</h2>
    <p>These protocols already trade. The board never ranks them: their market caps are the market's, not the model's. They are the comparables the size curve is fitted on.</p>
    <table id="live">
      <thead><tr><th>Protocol</th><th>Category</th><th class="num">TVL</th><th class="num">Market cap</th><th class="num">Multiple</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody id="liveRows"></tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="method">
    <h2>How the value is worked out</h2>
    <p><strong>Size curve.</strong> The 128 protocols in this snapshot whose token already trades are the comparables. A line is fitted through them in log space — log<sub>10</sub>(market cap) on log<sub>10</sub>(TVL) — and a pre-token protocol's curve value is read off that line at its own TVL. Big protocols carry a smaller multiple than small ones: the curve is concave, and the fit says so.</p>
    <p><strong>Growth and maturity.</strong> The curve value is multiplied by a growth factor from the protocol's seven-day TVL change (clamped to −50%…+100%, half weight) and a maturity factor from how long DefiLlama has tracked it with no token (0.80 for a newcomer, up to 1.00 after three years). No protocol's name ever matters: the same three numbers score every row.</p>
    <p><strong>What this radar does not claim.</strong> The snapshot carries no launch history, so no launch date is ever predicted and no protocol is said to have no token — only that its DefiLlama record carries none. The implied value is the entry's own claim: what a token would be worth if the protocol's record stayed as it is.</p>
    <h2>How the curve was tested</h2>
    <p>Four out-of-sample tests plus a 1000-round bootstrap, each against the same flat baseline (predict every comp at the median market-cap/TVL multiple). The table below is rendered from the model's own run, not typed in by hand — the numbers in it are the numbers the program computed from this snapshot.</p>
    <table id="valid">
